{"id": "school-district-high-risk-three-times", "title": "School district: rated high risk three times, one year with no audit opinion, costs up 60%", "seconds": 178.5, "voice": "elevenlabs:iPYqcpY8j8Ap4jUf28I3", "narrator": "Michael", "tempo": 1.2, "made": "2026-11-25", "key": "f3196c93a9d44408", "words": 431, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[5]"], "text": "How often did State watchdogs rate this district at high risk?", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 3.66, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "High risk of insolvency", "sub": "the State fiscal-crisis team"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.52, 0.72, 1.06, 1.65, 1.89, 2.05, 2.49, 2.59, 2.88]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[5]", "suspicious[0].what"], "text": "Three times in a row.", "t0": 3.66, "t1": 5.97, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "3", "label": "times rated high risk: 2022, 2024, 2026"}, "emph": ["Three"], "wt": [0.04, 0.97, 1.54, 1.74, 1.89]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "suspicious[0].why"], "text": "For 2022, the district’s own auditor gave no opinion. That means the books couldn’t be relied on.", "t0": 6.59, "t1": 12.98, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "No audit opinion, 2022", "chip": "$184 million federal money"}, "emph": ["no opinion"], "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.32, 1.24, 1.33, 1.79, 1.94, 2.45, 2.86, 3.02, 3.87, 4.65, 4.85, 5.01, 5.31, 5.53, 5.67, 6.04]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[15]"], "text": "Why? Payroll couldn’t be tested, and a 7.9 million dollar pay liability had no reconciliation.", "t0": 13.1, "t1": 19.04, "shot": "b6a", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "The auditor’s reasons, printed a year later", "sub": "payroll could not be tested after the new system", "chip": "$7.9 million, no reconciliation"}, "emph": ["7.9 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.92, 1.42, 1.65, 1.8, 2.37, 2.5, 2.57, 2.79, 3.08, 3.19, 3.57, 3.8, 4.06, 4.65, 4.85, 5.0]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[16]", "suspicious[0].what"], "text": "31 of 68 sampled relief charges had no documents.", "t0": 19.16, "t1": 23.64, "shot": "b6b", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$48.4 million", "label": "likely questioned costs, pandemic relief, 2021-22", "sub": "school meals: $17.8 million likely"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.41, 0.62, 1.2, 1.65, 1.95, 2.63, 3.17, 3.44]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[16]", "suspicious[0].what"], "text": "Likely questioned: 48.4 million dollars.", "t0": 23.76, "t1": 28.6, "shot": "b6b", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$48.4 million", "label": "likely questioned costs, pandemic relief, 2021-22", "sub": "school meals: $17.8 million likely"}, "emph": ["48.4 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.36, 1.6, 2.15, 2.75, 3.08, 3.99]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["established[6]", "suspicious[1]"], "text": "The State team’s review found 54 failings in 2022,", "t0": 28.72, "t1": 33.18, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Failing answers in the State review", "rows": [["2024", "64"], ["2026", "60"], ["2022", "54"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.43, 0.77, 1.23, 1.56, 2.19, 2.84, 3.0, 3.21]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["established[6]", "suspicious[1]"], "text": "64 in 2024, and 60 in 2026.", "t0": 33.18, "t1": 37.64, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Failing answers in the State review", "rows": [["2024", "64"], ["2026", "60"], ["2022", "54"]]}, "emph": ["64"], "wt": [0.04, 0.74, 0.96, 1.21, 2.05, 2.53, 3.05, 3.35, 3.56]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["story[3]"], "text": "Day-to-day spending rose from 777 million dollars to 1.24 billion.", "t0": 37.86, "t1": 44.13, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["spending, fiscal 2015", "$777 million"], "b": ["spending, fiscal 2024", "$1.24 billion"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.43, 0.89, 1.39, 1.71, 2.02, 2.31, 2.97, 3.39, 4.01, 4.35, 4.51, 4.84, 5.05, 5.42]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["story[3]", "oneLine", "established[19]"], "text": "Pupils fell 4 percent.", "t0": 44.25, "t1": 46.26, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "-4%", "label": "pupils, 59,105 to 56,508", "sub": "kindergarten applications: 4,968 to 3,835"}, "emph": ["4 percent"], "wt": [0.0, 0.57, 1.08, 1.45]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[2]"], "text": "Second, the central office: 1,679 dollars per pupil in 2024.", "t0": 46.88, "t1": 52.36, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["central office per pupil, SF", "$1,679"], "b": ["middle of like districts", "$1,128"]}, "emph": ["1,679"], "wt": [0.0, 0.54, 0.7, 0.99, 1.75, 1.84, 2.2, 2.42, 2.65, 3.18, 3.57, 3.76, 4.27, 4.44, 4.7]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "span", "ref": ["suspicious[3]"], "text": "The third lead is payroll. A new system went live in 2022.", "t0": 52.58, "t1": 56.72, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "span", "from": "2022-01-03", "to": "2025-07-01", "days": "1275", "fromLab": "new payroll system", "toLab": "replacement starts", "kicker": "The third lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.39, 0.69, 0.93, 1.9, 2.1, 2.25, 2.56, 2.72, 2.98, 3.09, 3.3]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what"], "text": "A repair contract grew by up to 8.8 million dollars. Then the system was replaced.", "t0": 56.84, "t1": 63.05, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Repair contract", "kicker": "The third lead", "chip": "up to $8,837,750"}, "emph": ["replaced"], "wt": [0.0, 0.04, 0.4, 0.98, 1.24, 1.4, 1.57, 1.67, 1.81, 2.21, 2.34, 2.93, 3.73, 4.28, 4.4, 5.0, 5.45]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[0]", "suspicious[3]"], "text": "The system’s own contract: 9.5 million in 2019,", "t0": 63.17, "t1": 67.39, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Infosys contract, October 2019", "$9.5 million"], "b": ["June 2022, after three raises", "$16,482,810"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.45, 0.62, 1.93, 2.14, 2.45, 2.61, 3.0, 3.12, 3.36]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[0]", "suspicious[3]"], "text": "raised three times to 16,482,810 by June 2022,", "t0": 67.39, "t1": 72.05, "shot": "b17x", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Infosys contract, October 2019", "$9.5 million"], "b": ["June 2022, after three raises", "$16,482,810"]}, "emph": ["16,482,810"], "wt": [0.04, 0.31, 0.62, 1.09, 1.18, 1.45, 1.86, 2.16, 2.33, 2.82, 3.06, 3.31, 3.57]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[0]", "suspicious[3]"], "text": "and amended again after.", "t0": 72.05, "t1": 73.4, "shot": "b17x", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Infosys contract, October 2019", "$9.5 million"], "b": ["June 2022, after three raises", "$16,482,810"]}, "wt": [0.04, 0.18, 0.53, 0.87]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "count", "ref": ["established[1]", "established[20]"], "text": "And in those payroll years, the district certified itself positive in all 4 interim reports.", "t0": 73.52, "t1": 79.07, "shot": "b17a", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "4 of 4", "label": "interim reports the district certified positive, 2021-22 and 2022-23", "sub": "the State later listed it negative 3 times"}, "emph": ["all 4"], "wt": [0.0, 0.06, 0.18, 0.34, 0.75, 1.44, 1.52, 1.86, 2.27, 2.62, 3.26, 3.55, 3.85, 4.27, 4.7]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[12]", "suspicious[0].what"], "text": "In 2021-22,", "t0": 79.19, "t1": 81.46, "shot": "b17b", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$35.9 million", "label": "pandemic relief reported as professional and technical services, 2021-22", "sub": "third round $19,257,728; second round $16,630,631"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.06, 0.4, 0.99, 1.24]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[12]", "suspicious[0].what"], "text": "35.9 million dollars of pandemic relief went on professional and technical services.", "t0": 81.46, "t1": 87.69, "shot": "b17b", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$35.9 million", "label": "pandemic relief reported as professional and technical services, 2021-22", "sub": "third round $19,257,728; second round $16,630,631"}, "emph": ["35.9 million"], "wt": [0.04, 0.61, 0.98, 1.21, 1.74, 2.26, 2.4, 2.9, 3.5, 3.92, 4.06, 4.69, 4.98, 5.43]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[14]", "suspicious[3].what"], "text": "The State’s pay files show no district rows after 2021, or for 2020, before the new system.", "t0": 87.81, "t1": 94.12, "shot": "b17d", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "The State Controller’s pay files", "sub": "no district rows for 2020, 2022, 2023 or 2024"}, "emph": ["after 2021"], "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.41, 0.62, 1.0, 1.22, 1.4, 1.82, 2.12, 2.33, 2.59, 3.76, 3.94, 4.13, 4.4, 5.25, 5.46, 5.59, 5.76]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "count", "ref": ["established[17]", "suspicious[3].what"], "text": "Later audits found payroll weak every year. Someone inside redirected four pay deposits.", "t0": 94.24, "t1": 100.26, "shot": "b17e", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "4", "label": "payroll deposits redirected by someone inside the district, 2023-24", "sub": "audit findings: 11, 7 and 10 a year since 2022-23"}, "emph": ["four pay deposits"], "wt": [0.0, 0.26, 0.59, 0.86, 1.29, 1.69, 2.15, 2.73, 3.61, 4.07, 4.67, 4.95, 5.21]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4]"], "text": "The fourth lead: contracts approved after the work began.", "t0": 100.48, "t1": 104.08, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Approved after the work began", "kicker": "The fourth lead"}, "wt": [0.01, 0.08, 0.49, 1.0, 1.76, 2.29, 2.58, 2.68, 2.99]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4]"], "text": "Here, retroactive means the work began before the board voted.", "t0": 104.2, "t1": 107.67, "shot": "ratification", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Work already performed", "sub": "Retroactive approval"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.48, 1.05, 1.29, 1.39, 1.67, 2.07, 2.5, 2.65, 2.93]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what"], "text": "336 board items call a contract retroactive.", "t0": 107.79, "t1": 112.67, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "336", "label": "agenda items calling a contract retroactive, since January 2018"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.66, 1.44, 1.77, 2.36, 2.77, 2.87, 3.63]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[8]", "story[11]"], "text": "The fifth lead: the budget. Its own forms flagged 15 items in June 2024,", "t0": 112.89, "t1": 119.82, "shot": "b19a0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "The budget", "kicker": "The fifth lead", "sub": "items flagged in the district’s own budget forms"}, "emph": ["15 items"], "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.51, 1.19, 1.81, 2.59, 3.39, 3.61, 4.04, 4.39, 4.8, 5.18, 5.32, 5.57, 5.84]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[9]", "story[9]", "established[18]"], "text": "The unaudited figure: 428.9 million.", "t0": 119.82, "t1": 124.62, "shot": "b19b", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["forecast, end of 2024-25 (June 2024)", "$187.1 million"], "b": ["audited balance, 2024-25", "$428,923,463"]}, "emph": ["428.9 million"], "wt": [0.04, 0.21, 0.73, 1.71, 1.91, 2.21, 2.91, 3.46, 3.79]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[9]"], "text": "241.9 million dollars more than budgeted.", "t0": 124.74, "t1": 129.89, "shot": "b19c", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$241.9 million", "label": "more than budgeted"}, "emph": ["241.9"], "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.68, 1.66, 2.01, 2.42, 3.14, 3.79, 4.31, 4.51]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[10]"], "text": "Yet the June 2026 budget projects spending above revenue", "t0": 130.41, "t1": 134.1, "shot": "b19d", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "in 2028-29, the District is projected to have its Unrestricted General Fund expenditures exceed its revenues by $26 million."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.28, 0.6, 0.92, 1.48, 1.96, 2.59, 2.94, 3.27]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[10]"], "text": "by 26 million dollars in 2028-29.", "t0": 134.1, "t1": 138.64, "shot": "b19d", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "in 2028-29, the District is projected to have its Unrestricted General Fund expenditures exceed its revenues by $26 million."}, "emph": ["26 million"], "wt": [0.04, 0.31, 0.86, 1.42, 2.17, 2.44, 2.76, 3.37, 3.76]}, {"scene": "record", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[21]"], "text": "The parcel-tax auditor could not verify two sampled exemptions for seniors.", "t0": 138.86, "t1": 143.21, "shot": "record-21-2 of 60 exemptions", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "w25q2", "text": "2 of 60 exemptions", "mark": "2 of 60 exemptions", "kicker": "San Francisco Unified School District"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.74, 1.13, 1.41, 1.62, 2.11, 2.41, 2.87, 3.39, 3.56]}, {"scene": "record", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[22]"], "text": "State advisers gained power to stay or rescind board actions threatening financial stability.", "t0": 143.33, "t1": 148.73, "shot": "record-22-May 2024", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "fb2", "text": "May 2024", "mark": "May 2024", "kicker": "San Francisco Unified School District"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.69, 0.93, 1.31, 1.48, 1.89, 2.13, 2.64, 2.93, 3.46, 4.12, 4.65]}, {"scene": "record", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[24]"], "text": "The district moved costs from unrestricted to restricted resources to help balance the books.", "t0": 148.85, "t1": 155.07, "shot": "record-24-$48.3 million", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "fb8", "text": "$48.3 million", "mark": "$48.3 million", "kicker": "San Francisco Unified School District"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.63, 1.11, 1.61, 1.88, 2.71, 2.95, 3.62, 4.44, 4.93, 5.15, 5.59, 5.75]}, {"scene": "record", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[25]"], "text": "The board’s draft annual audit and the signed report differed on questioned costs.", "t0": 155.19, "t1": 159.99, "shot": "record-25-February 2025", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "i11a", "text": "February 2025", "mark": "February 2025", "kicker": "San Francisco Unified School District"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.43, 0.75, 1.11, 1.55, 1.72, 1.82, 2.19, 2.78, 3.48, 3.74, 4.19]}, {"scene": "record", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[26]"], "text": "Retirement savings depended on how many positions the district kept vacant.", "t0": 160.11, "t1": 163.71, "shot": "record-26-352 employees", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "fb12", "text": "352 employees", "mark": "352 employees", "kicker": "San Francisco Unified School District"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.49, 0.94, 1.28, 1.42, 1.59, 1.75, 2.27, 2.41, 2.81, 3.03]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "The records don’t show any money was misused. Or the full cost of the payroll system.", "t0": 163.93, "t1": 168.25, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That any money was misused", "The full cost of the payroll system"]}, "wt": [0.24, 0.31, 0.41, 0.63, 0.9, 1.08, 1.3, 1.51, 2.31, 2.57, 2.71, 2.95, 3.29, 3.36, 3.45, 3.8]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]"], "text": "What would settle it?", "t0": 168.37, "t1": 169.17, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "The 2021-22 audit report"}, {"who": "", "what": "The full payroll-system cost"}, {"who": "", "what": "Any repayment of questioned costs"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.26, 0.53]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]"], "text": "The 2021-22 audit itself, the full payroll bill, and what was repaid.", "t0": 169.17, "t1": 175.12, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "The 2021-22 audit report"}, {"who": "", "what": "The full payroll-system cost"}, {"who": "", "what": "Any repayment of questioned costs"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.04, 0.53, 0.79, 1.33, 1.59, 2.02, 2.43, 3.24, 3.34, 3.61, 4.09, 4.84, 4.93, 5.14, 5.34]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "Every source is linked in the case file below.", "t0": 175.24, "t1": 177.61, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.67, 0.81, 1.11, 1.17, 1.29, 1.61, 1.9]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The finding", "found": "What was found", "lead1": "Lead 1 · cost", "lead2": "Lead 2 · central office", "lead3": "Lead 3 · payroll", "lead4": "Lead 4 · after the fact", "lead5": "Lead 5 · the budgets", "close": "Where it stands", "record": "The public record"}, "look": "newsroom", "hook": "question"}